# Don't

- Do not bypass pre-commit hooks (`--no-verify`, `SKIP=...`).
- Do not embed ticket/issue IDs in source comments — use plain-language rationale.
- Do not add repo-root `reports/` — use `.shipgate/reports/`.
- Do not edit bundled catalog for repo-specific paths or thresholds.
- Do not add allowlist entries without an exceptional, documented reason (see `quality.mdc` Dogfooding).
- Do not delete dead code by commenting out — delete it.
- Do not inline Python in shell gates — use `src/shipgate/gates/` helpers (see `gates.mdc`).
- Hook output: pass/fail only; actionable stderr on failure.
